{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00146 - MONDO_1068",
  "verbalization": "Calcifediol is implicated in the pathogenesis of Osteomalacia (disease) through a multi-step mechanism involving the induction of Rickets and subsequent progression to Osteomalacia. The evidence suggests that Calcifediol, through its indication for Rickets, acts as a precursor in the metabolic pathway that leads to Osteomalacia. This is supported by the indication of Dihydrotachysterol, a related compound, as a mediator in the transition from Rickets to Osteomalacia. The presence of Calcifediol as an off-label use for Rickets further strengthens the link, as it implies a therapeutic role in the condition. The integrated evidence suggests that Calcifediol may influence the biochemical processes underlying Osteomalacia, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores indicate a strong, though not absolute, association between Calcifediol and Osteomalacia, supported by the sequential indications of Rickets and Dihydrotachysterol.",
